Mumcord on FreeBSD uses the graphics driver that is loaded.

Intel graphics (Comet Lake, and other Gen9/Gen12 chips) need drm-66-kmod:

    pkg delete drm-612-kmod drm-kmod
    pkg install drm-66-kmod
    reboot

With drm-612-kmod (the default the drm-kmod metaport selects) these GPUs hang
with "rcs0 preemption time out" and take the whole desktop down with them, not
just Mumcord (freebsd/drm-kmod issue #509).

To check which renderer Mumcord got:

    LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=0 glxinfo -B        # "Mesa Intel(R) ..." = hardware

Running Mumcord with LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1 forces software rendering
(llvmpipe) if the driver turns out to be unusable.
